title Mycelium Chorus r1 — a quorum of independent Vouchers, a position believed when distinct nodes agree
prompt baton prin recur — read REMEMBER + the 1,024-round itinerary + the six-season double-seat, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, approve own design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop at custody gates.
think Read REMEMBER (git nib 541b2b9f94), the 1,024-round itinerary, and the six-season double-seat expansion. The tree stands far past the itinerary's fixed rows — Seasons 1–3 (TACT · Yield · Commons) are complete across every agent-doable rung and the frontier is a deep Season D Mycelium arc: Cord · gossip · fact-batching · Knot · Tenure · Till · Purse · Pledge · Braid · Lapse · Statement · Voucher, each a signed primitive with a four-rung shape (r1 crux · r2 travels · r3 across a Knot · r4 true to the bytes). HEAD ea7f351a07 folded the Voucher arc onto REMEMBER; working tree clean.
think Sought the genuine highest-Lindy crux rather than another near-identical arc. Read voucher.rye and voucher_bron.rye: the Voucher makes a position PROVABLE under one node's signature, yet a verifier who does not hold the blocks must simply TRUST that the single signing node read the ledger true — one node can sign a position it never honestly derived; the offline check confirms the signature is well-formed, not that the reading was true. That is the blind spot the whole ledger set has carried since the first Voucher: a single attestation is only as trustworthy as its single author. The fault-tolerant completion is a quorum — the heart the double-seat's own Mycelium-consensus vision named (improving on TigerBeetle/Mysticeti). That is Lindy (a mesh becomes trustworthy to a stranger when a reading rests on many independent voices, not one) and crux-first (the hard-but-tractable move: a threshold law over a bounded set of independent Vouchers, distinct-signer-enforced so one node cannot manufacture a quorum).
think Named the journey the Chorus (comlink-tendency: clear/warm/safe; grep-clean of any seated module or waymark — appears only as unchosen round-history in the Verse Lexicon note; parses as no @p; sits true beside the ledger's own voice motif — ledger-voice, account-voice — a chorus being the many voices whose agreement makes a reading believed). Wrote the self-approved design read (active-designing/20260813-102533_…) naming the four-rung arc: r1 quorum-law crux · r2 travels (chorus_bron, a format chorus-v1 with member-tagged voucher blocks) · r3 across a Knot · r4 true to the bytes.
think Implemented r1 (mycelium/chorus.rye): the Chorus carries one CLAIM (order-head · account · position) and up to chorus_max_members (16) member Vouchers. open(dag, account) sets the claim to the true reading (voucher.order_head_of + lapse.resolve + statement.statement_for); add(dag, node_kp) gathers one node's independent voice via voucher.make_voucher; add_voucher appends a voice made elsewhere (or, in the witness, a forged/disagreeing one to refuse). The crux verify_chorus(threshold) folds four laws in order — every member verifies offline (else BadSignature); every member agrees on the one claim (else Disagreement); the signers are distinct, pairwise (a repeated node → DuplicateNode, so one voice cannot inflate the count); the distinct count meets the threshold (else BelowThreshold). check_against(dag) re-derives the head and re-reads the Statement once and confirms the one claim is true. Two contract asserts per function with positive // invariant: lines, explicit widths (u32 counts, u64 positions), named errors, copy_disjoint over memcpy.
obs GREEN on the first build and run across five scenes: open (three distinct nodes vouch Alice's balance 0/reserved 100/received 100; believed at threshold 3 and 2, refuses BelowThreshold at 4; checks against the ledger), posted (reserved 0, believed at 2), lapsed (coins home, balance 100, believed at the full 3), arrival-independence inherited (a chorus gathered against one round-2 permutation verifies and checks against the other — every honest member folds to one order-head and reads one position), and the quorum-law refusals: BelowThreshold (two distinct voices cannot meet a threshold of three), DuplicateNode (the same node vouching twice cannot inflate two voices to three — Sybil-by-repetition refused), Disagreement (a voice honestly made against a different — open — ledger has a valid signature yet names a different head/position, so it refuses rather than blur two readings), BadSignature (a forged voice with its balance flipped breaks its own signature). The rendered open chorus reads voices=3.
obs Additive discipline held: composed voucher+cord+fold+lapse+statement+kumara public API only, edited no module, each re-runs GREEN at the witness door. The member set is bounded at chorus_max_members and the distinct-signer check walks it pairwise — bounded, no unbounded walk. First-pass cleanup before building: moved the fold import into the top triad and replaced two orelse-unreachable demo helpers with voucher.rye's own named-error mint pattern in seat_scene. TAME style bans clean; width-check exit 0. Demo node/keeper seeds — no key/funds/network/custody; a served chorus reaches the Comlink-served gate.
loom witness=mycelium_chorus_witness scenes=5 max_members=16 refusals=4 first_run=green
